/* ── The dashboard parts: what the package leaves to a register [kpadopt2-repairs] ──
   Formal keeps these parts exactly as Kenny approved them; this theme takes the three repairs the review asks for: a
   loading heat grid or matrix row as tall as its ready row (no skeleton gap between cells), an empty or failed run
   timeline with a lane-sized space for its sentence (never over the legend), the sentence as wide as its words on the
   theme's ground (never through a rule or a ghost bar), and an axis label near the end edge standing before its rule. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The six opt-in options of the dashboard adoption, round 3, in this theme [kpadopt3] ──
   The nav bar's separator, the timeline's day buttons and series runs, the week agenda's upcoming list on a phone and
   the facet swatch's identity pattern (the choice-filter value and the heat grid's End are behaviour only).
   Cyberpunk's own (themes/cyberpunk/CHARACTER.md): the separator is the neon slash, the yellow leaning with
   the bar's own cut and split into its cyan ghost (the RGB split); lying down in the phone's list it is a short data
   dash on the plate, yellow then a cyan packet, never wider than the plate. A day on the axis takes the RGB split under
   the pointer; pressed it is a lock-on: the yellow ground with its notched corner and the hard yellow foot. A series'
   finished run has the hard 3 px bar on its leading edge, as a week pill does; the facet pattern is notched. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── The kpadopt4 components in cyberpunk's own grammar [kpadopt4] ──
   Cyberpunk is the netrunner's HUD (themes/cyberpunk/CHARACTER.md): the void is the ground, the holo card what stands on
   it, the HUD what the system draws over it. A signal is acquired, never eased: a part that is drawn is torn in sideways
   and jitters home in six ticks of 60 ms, held poses with `steps(1)` (G1, G3, G12); pointing lights the 14 px circuit in
   its own ink in one tick (G8); a press lights it full (G14); a warning is locked as a target, four corner brackets, 2 px,
   in the tone's ink (G13); the machine talks in prefixed mono capitals, figures in the condensed display (G15); a
   control is cut at its end corner, a plate at its dossier corner, never rounded (G6). Yellow acts, cyan reads, red
   alarms. Waiting is the reticle's lock-on the register already lays; the data stream is only for what is transferred. */
@layer kp.signature {

/* ── end the kpadopt4 data pieces ── */

